# Generics Basics 🧬

Generics allow you to write functions, classes, or interfaces that work over a variety of types rather than a single one, while **preserving exact type information**:

```typescript
// <T> captures the exact input type!
function getFirstElement<T>(arr: T[]): T | undefined {
  return arr[0];
}

const num = getFirstElement([10, 20, 30]);      // Inferred as number!
const str = getFirstElement(["A", "B", "C"]);    // Inferred as string!

console.log("First number:", num);
console.log("First string:", str);
```

