# Multiple Generic Parameters 🔀

Functions can accept multiple generic type arguments:

```typescript
function createPair<K, V>(key: K, value: V): [K, V] {
  return [key, value];
}

const pair1 = createPair("userID", 1004); // [string, number]
const pair2 = createPair(true, ["Admin", "Root"]); // [boolean, string[]]

console.log("Pair 1:", pair1);
console.log("Pair 2:", pair2);
```

