# Type Narrowing with the `in` Operator 🚪

Check if a specific property exists on an object union:

```typescript
type Fish = { swim: () => void };
type Bird = { fly: () => void };

function move(animal: Fish | Bird) {
  if ("swim" in animal) {
    animal.swim(); // Narrowed to Fish!
  } else {
    animal.fly();  // Narrowed to Bird!
  }
}

move({ swim: () => console.log("Swimming...") });
move({ fly: () => console.log("Flying...") });
```

