# Intersection Types (`&`) 🔀

Combine multiple existing types into one comprehensive type:

```typescript
type Auditable = {
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  version: number;
};

type Post = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  content: string;
};

type AuditablePost = Post & Auditable;

const myPost: AuditablePost = {
  id: "P1",
  title: "TypeScript Deep Dive",
  content: "Advanced Types...",
  createdAt: new Date(),
  updatedAt: new Date(),
  version: 1
};

console.log("Auditable Post:", myPost.title, "v" + myPost.version);
```

