# Type Extraction with `infer` 🕵️

The `infer` keyword allows you to extract and deduce a type from inside another type:

```typescript
// Unpacks the item type T from an array T[]
type Flatten<T> = T extends Array<infer ItemType> ? ItemType : T;

type StrArray = Flatten<string[]>; // Inferred as string!
type PlainNumber = Flatten<number>; // Inferred as number!

console.log("Inferred array item extraction demonstrated.");
```

