# Template Literal Types 💬

Construct new string types using template literal syntax:

```typescript
type EventType = "click" | "hover" | "focus";
type ElementType = "button" | "input";

// Produces "button_click" | "button_hover" | "input_click" ...
type InteractionEvent = `${ElementType}_${EventType}`;

const eventA: InteractionEvent = "button_click"; // Valid!
// const eventB: InteractionEvent = "div_click"; // Error!

console.log("Interaction Event:", eventA);
```

