# Mapped Types 🗺️

Build new types by transforming each property in an existing type:

```typescript
type FeatureFlags = {
  darkMode: boolean;
  betaAccess: boolean;
  twoFactorAuth: boolean;
};

// Make all properties readonly using a mapped type:
type ReadonlyFlags<T> = {
  readonly [K in keyof T]: T[K];
};

const flags: ReadonlyFlags<FeatureFlags> = {
  darkMode: true,
  betaAccess: false,
  twoFactorAuth: true
};

// flags.darkMode = false; // Error: Cannot assign to 'darkMode'
console.log("Flags:", flags);
```

